# Cataclysm 0.9 — Living Horde implementation

Status: implemented source; NOT release-approved. Browser acceptance could not launch in this sandbox. Published game/dashboard byte verification and independent QA remain outstanding; do not replace the accepted published 0.9 based on this report.

Read job.json, plan.json (including update_decision.selection), feedback.md (empty array) and CATACLYSM_1_0_ROADMAP.md. Inspected the existing preview runtime before editing. No private recordings were accessed. No frozen baseline, metadata, dependencies, tests, workflows, dashboard or publishing code were edited.

## Selected features and concrete changes

- **designer**: game.js now contains one Threat Director integrated into tick/spawnEnemy, and one mutation implementation integrated into movement, collision damage and rendering. Rolling actual kills and capped effective damage use a 12-second exponential average. Level contributes modestly; proximity, alive weighted threat, recent damage and frame pressure constrain replenishment. Budget starts at 12 and smoothly approaches a target clamped to 12–38 (20-second response). Species cost 1–3 threat; larger shamblers cost 1.5×, mutations add 1, bosses cost 12. Budget exhaustion blocks spawning until below 72% and nearby population below five; nine nearby enemies block it. Damage grants five seconds without ordinary spawns. Attempt intervals remain 0.55–2.8 seconds, with no catch-up bursts. Live cap is min(configured cap,72), alongside the existing 160-shot ceiling and capped trails/fish/particles. A smoothed browser frame interval above 38ms stops ordinary replenishment until below 28ms; existing 50ms simulation-step cap remains.
- Bosses retain five-minute milestones, species, rewards and scaling. They reserve budget by withdrawing distant ordinary enemies without kill credit or drops, then grant four seconds of recovery. If surviving Kings already occupy the available boss budget, another King is deferred to a later milestone. This deliberate safety exception prevents unlimited accumulated bosses.
- After 360 seconds, eligible ordinary spawns have an 18% mutation chance, six-second shared cooldown, maximum two concurrent mutations and eight-second lifetime. Bosses never mutate. Orange **RUSH!** provides a one-second slowed wind-up followed by a committed 0.6-second rush; sidestep it. Blue **◇** warns for one second before halving incoming damage; kite until expiry (never invulnerable). Pink **≈** visibly marks slower sinusoidal weaving; ordinary shots and positioning counter it. One mutation per enemy, no permanent speed/HP stacking. Rings and text work with reduced motion; no flashing is required. index.html explains counters.
- **researcher**: player shots roll critical chance once when created: 6% + 0.4 percentage points per level beyond one + 1.2 percentage points per damage above baseline, capped at 22%. Critical damage is 1.75×, retained on ricochets; expected extra damage is bounded to 16.5%. Critical projectiles have a gold ring/spark and gold impact particles, with no new particle pool. Companion attacks retain their existing damage. No precision/stealth bonus was invented because those systems do not exist.

## Interfaces and preservation

Internal frozen `ThreatDirector.getThreatBudget()` returns the actual current budget. `SpawnManager.spawnEnemy(type, mutationFlags)` returns an enemy or null when safety rules block it; optional `{type:'burst'|'shield'|'weave'}` selects a mutation only after ordinary eligibility/rarity checks. Every ordinary EnemyObject has `applyMutation(type,duration)`, clamping duration to 1–10 seconds; spawn policy is the only runtime caller. Player Shot objects implement `calculateDamage()` and `isCriticalHit()`; collision consumes the former, then applies shield mitigation. `Renderer.drawCriticalHitEffect(shot)` renders only marked shots. These helpers remain internal; no mutable debug API was added. Existing read-only CATACLYSM_DIAGNOSTICS now copies director counters, mutation state, costs and shot critical/damage fields.

BUILD, expected boot version and game-version remain **0.9**; technical PATCH_ID is **42523008693-1-living-horde**. Local script/style query stamps and visible build marker use this run ID. Stable docs/preview location is unchanged. Existing controls, keyboard/pointer cancellation, sound, squad tactics, companion recruitment/abilities, relics, offers/XP/upgrades and responsive CSS remain in place. Only game.js and index.html changed in the target; configuration and CSS are unchanged.

## Commands and evidence

- `node --check docs/preview/game.js`: PASS.
- `git diff --check`: PASS.
- `node /tmp/horde-test.cjs`: PASS. Full reproducible test source is included below; it runs the actual game closure in a Node VM with DOM/canvas/audio stubs and test-only access injected into an in-memory copy. It never edits production diagnostics or source state for acceptance tests. Tests explicitly set high HP/invulnerability to isolate endurance/bounds; these are NOT evidence of natural survival balance.
- Three deterministic 780-second runs at 50ms steps: no-fire crowded field, baseline damage plus squad, and high-DPS build plus squad. All reached two boss encounters. Maximum enemies: 10/13/4; shots: 0/20/49. Spawns: 10/431/1110. Upgrade choices: 0/14/27. Both firing runs encountered all three mutations and all species unlocked through stalker. Natural runs had at most one mutation alive; a targeted two-enemy mutation test covers concurrent expiry. Zero-fire population stayed bounded and suppressed replenishment rather than gaining unlocked enemies atop a full field.
- Fixed-input response test: low effectiveness budget 12, delay 1.65s; sustained high effectiveness budget 16.804, delay 0.962s after 25 seconds. Crowded budget and damage-recovery suppress spawns. Early species and pre-six-minute mutation exclusion asserted. All mutation types expired; burst warning pace asserted. Actual collision test produced 7 damage from a critical base-4 shot and 3.5 against an active shield. Critical frequency test: 597/10000 at baseline chance. All three upgrade choice indices, companion abilities, slow relic activation, pause-time freeze/resume, clean restart and frame-pressure suppression exercised.
- Simulation CPU time for 15,600 ticks per scenario was approximately 0.36/0.70/0.54 seconds on this runner. This excludes real rendering and is NOT mobile FPS evidence. A stub render smoke check executed without exceptions; it does NOT validate visual appearance or viewport geometry.
- `node game_factory/mobile_acceptance.cjs`: BLOCKED before page load. Chrome exited SIGTRAP after `crashpad/util/linux/socket.cc: setsockopt: Operation not permitted`. The supplied check was not modified. No gate.log existed on initial inspection. No browser retry or claimed gate pass.

## Remaining limitations and next cycle

Browser/mobile validation is still required at 640×320, 844×390 and portrait: real drag, release/cancel, start/pause/resume/restart, rune/ability buttons, all upgrade cards, mutation and critical legibility, performance and dialog reachability. No physical-phone testing, live deployment, dashboard fetch, rollback publication or independent QA approval occurred. No acceptance claim is made for those criteria. Natural survival balance and frame-pressure recovery need real playtesting; simulations establish bounded mechanics, not that deaths are avoidable in every encounter. Existing elapsed-time species unlock schedule remains intact; measured effectiveness changes pressure gradually rather than abruptly unlocking extra species.

Deferred: engineer's duplicate mutation implementation (designer provides the single source), power-gated species unlocks, further late-run discoveries/environmental encounters and building collision/pathfinding. These roadmap ideas need separate selection and profiling; viewer suggestions are not treated as verified bugs. No additional inferred private-evidence claims were introduced.

